            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Once fully cured, most impregnating stone sealers sold for kitchen countertops are described by their makers as safe for food-contact surfaces, because the active ingredient sits inside the stone rather than on the surface. Check the specific product's label or data sheet, and keep the surface clear until the cure time has passed."
          }
