            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Unsealed marble absorbs oil, wine, coffee and colored foods quickly, so stains become more likely and harder to remove. It will not crack or deteriorate from a lack of sealer. Some very dense polished marbles absorb so slowly they rarely need sealing at all, which is why testing matters more than routine."
