          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Sealing marble well comes down to three habits: test before you seal, keep the stone wet only while it is soaking, and wipe it completely dry before anything can cure on top. The product matters less than those steps, though a good impregnator from our <a href="/best-marble-sealer/">marble sealer roundup</a> will last longer between treatments.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then let the water test, not the calendar, tell you when to do it again, and remember that sealing is stain insurance only. Acids will still etch, so wipe spills promptly and keep a polishing compound for the marks that get through.
          </p>
